                <pb facs="0352" n="240" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg240"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Hill to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-12-24"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 24,
                    1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Hill reports that the German foreign office telephones that it fully agrees
                    to the general principles laid down in Mr. Hitt’s memorandum embodying telegram
                    of November 6, and will reply in writing after Christmas.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
